SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.RSCH #c8-stuck-newversion: publishV2 recovers a Zenodo newversion draft that refuses new files (goal research-exec-newversion-draft-cleanup)',
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-research-exec/worker.js
code-anchor: async function publishV2(env, row) {
code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-research-exec/worker.js"], "contains": "stuck-newversion"}
Charter pillar: research. Program QNFO.RSCH. Goal research-exec-newversion-draft-cleanup (adopted since 2026-09-15; its machine check is the same code-probe). Defect: when Zenodo answers a newversion request for a concept with 400 files.enabled "remove all files first", publishV2 has no branch that finds the existing draft of the concept, clears or reuses it and carries on, so the paper waits for manual Zenodo intervention. Read 2026-11-05: qnfo-research-exec/worker.js has no stuck-draft handling and no test for it (the only newversion text is the queued-newversion event at publishV2''s caller); no cloud_ops_events text since 2026-10-28 carries the Zenodo message, so the defect is latent, not recurring. Next action: in publishV2, when the newversion call returns 400 with that message, list the concept''s draft deposits (GET the concept''s versions with status draft), reuse or delete the draft''s files and retry once; log a stuck-newversion event; bump VERSION with worker_release.py; add a test that stubs the 400 and asserts one retry and the event. Definition of done: the code-probe above reads present on main, the new test passes, and a stubbed 400 produces exactly one retry. Metric to move: zenodo_versions_per_flagship (guard: publications_30d not lower). Prediction: 0 papers wait on a stuck newversion draft; today the count is unmeasured.',
 'claude-session', 'reliability', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.RSCH #c8-stuck-newversion:%' AND status NOT IN ('closed', 'resolved'));
